msgid ""
"The <i>p</i>-value is %1$s and the null hypothesis of equal %2$s across "
"protected groups %3$s. %4$s"
msgstr ""
"<i>p</i>値は %1$s であり、保護された群のあいだで %2$s が等しいという帰無仮説"
"は %3$s。%4$s"

msgid ""
"The goal of this procedure is to determine to what extent the predictions of "
"an algorithm are fair towards protected groups on a sensitive attribute. "
"Fairness -or discrimination- can be quantified using so-called fairness "
"measures. There are various fairness measures, and different measures can "
"lead to different conclusions about fairness. Therefore, selecting the most "
"appropriate fairness measure for the context at hand is crucial. The "
"decision-making workflow allows for determining the most suitable fairness "
"measure by answering the necessary questions."
msgstr ""
"この手順の目的は、あるアルゴリズムの予測が、センシティブ属性にもとづく保護対"
"象の群に対してどの程度公平かを判定することです。公平性(あるいは差別)はいわゆ"
"る公平性指標で数値化できます。公平性指標にはさまざまなものがあり、指標が違え"
"ば公平性についての結論も変わりえます。そのため、その場面に最も適した公平性指"
"標を選ぶことが決定的に重要です。意思決定の流れに沿って必要な問いに答えていく"
"ことで、最も適した公平性指標を決められます。"

msgid "<u>Selection</u>"
msgstr "<u>選択</u>"

msgid "<u>Evaluation</u>"
msgstr "<u>評価</u>"

msgid "The most suitable fairness measure is <b>%1$s</b>."
msgstr "最も適した公平性指標は <b>%1$s</b>です。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same ratio of items from two "
"different groups experiencing a change in the status quo (i.e., being "
"classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being classified; "
"these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such as bank "
"accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Disparate impact is obtained by dividing the positive rate of the "
"unprivileged group by that of the privileged group. The positive rate is "
"equal to (TP+FP)/N, where TP denotes true positives (items correctly "
"classified as positive), FP denotes false positives (items incorrectly "
"classified as positive), and N represents the total number of items "
"classified by the algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"The most common use of disparate impact is linked to the U.S. Equal "
"Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) guidelines, particularly the %1$s%% "
"rule. According to this rule, if disparate impact is higher than 0.80, there "
"is no discrimination. This method has limitations, as the threshold value is "
"not based on the measure's properties, data characteristics, or statistical "
"considerations. Originally derived from U.S. employment hiring rates, the "
"rule lacks theoretical rigor for broader applications."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状の変化を経験する(すな"
"わち陽性と分類される)対象の割合が、2つの異なる群のあいだで等しくなることです"
"。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合もあれば"
"、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"不均衡影響は、非特権群の陽性率を特権群の陽性率で割って求めます。陽性率は "
"(TP+FP)/N です。ここで TP は真陽性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)、FP は偽陽性"
"(誤って陽性と分類された対象)、N はアルゴリズムが分類した対象の総数を表します"
"。\n"
"\n"
"<u>補足:</u>\n"
"不均衡影響の最も一般的な用法は、米国雇用機会均等委員会 (EEOC) の指針、とくに "
"%1$s%% ルールに結びついています。このルールによれば、不均衡影響が 0.80 を上回"
"れば差別はないとされます。ただし、このしきい値は指標の性質・データの特徴・統"
"計的な考察にもとづくものではないという限界があります。もともと米国の雇用にお"
"ける採用率から導かれたものであり、より広い場面に適用するには理論的な厳密さを"
"欠いています。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct and incorrect changes in the status "
"quo (i.e, being, correctly and incorrectly, classified as positive). The "
"term items refers to what is being classified; these items can be people, "
"like job applicants, or objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Equalized odds combines the true positive rate (TPR) and the false positive "
"rate (FPR). The TPR is calculated as TP/(TP+FP) and the FPR as FP/(TN+FP), "
"applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes true "
"positives (correctly classified positive items), TN denotes true negatives "
"(correctly classified negative items), and FP denotes false positives "
"(incorrectly classified positive items).\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"It is important to note that this is the only measure in the decision-making "
"workflow that addresses both the correct classification of the positive "
"class and the incorrect classification of the negative class."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状の正しい変化と誤った"
"変化(すなわち正しく陽性と分類されること、および誤って陽性と分類されること)を"
"経験する対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等しくなることです。ここでいう「対象」"
"とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合もあれば、銀行口座のような物"
"の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"オッズの均等化は、真陽性率 (TPR) と偽陽性率 (FPR) を組み合わせたものです。"
"TPR は TP/(TP+FP)、FPR は FP/(TN+FP) として、特権群と非特権群の両方について計"
"算します。ここで TP は真陽性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)、TN は真陰性(正しく"
"陰性と分類された対象)、FP は偽陽性(誤って陽性と分類された対象)を表します。\n"
"\n"
"<u>補足:</u>\n"
"この指標は、意思決定の流れの中で唯一、陽性クラスの正しい分類と陰性クラスの誤"
"った分類の両方を扱うものである点に注意してください。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct changes in the status quo (i.e., being "
"correctly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being "
"classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such "
"as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Predictive rate parity is based on precision, calculated as TP/(TP+FP), "
"applied to both the privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes "
"true positives (correctly classified positive items) and FP denotes false "
"positives (incorrectly classified positive items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状の正しい変化(すなわち"
"正しく陽性と分類されること)を経験する対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等しくなる"
"ことです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合"
"もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"的中率の等価性は適合率にもとづき、TP/(TP+FP) として特権群と非特権群の両方につ"
"いて計算します。ここで TP は真陽性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)、FP は偽陽性"
"(誤って陽性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing correct changes in the status quo (i.e., being "
"correctly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is being "
"classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or objects, such "
"as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Equal opportunity is based on the true positive rate, calculated as TP/"
"(TP+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP "
"denotes true positives (correctly classified positive items) and FN denotes "
"false negatives (incorrectly classified negative items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状の正しい変化(すなわち"
"正しく陽性と分類されること)を経験する対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等しくなる"
"ことです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合"
"もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"機会の均等は真陽性率にもとづき、TP/(TP+FN) として特権群と非特権群の両方につい"
"て計算します。ここで TP は真陽性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)、FN は偽陰性(誤"
"って陰性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Specificity parity is based on the true negative rate, calculated as TN/"
"(TN+FP), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TN "
"denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative items) and FP denotes "
"false positives (incorrectly classified positive items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状が正しく変わらないま"
"ま(すなわち正しく陰性と分類されること)である対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等"
"しくなることです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような"
"人の場合もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"特異度の等価性は真陰性率にもとづき、TN/(TN+FP) として特権群と非特権群の両方に"
"ついて計算します。ここで TN は真陰性(正しく陰性と分類された対象)、FP は偽陽性"
"(誤って陽性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Negative predictive value parity is based on the negative predictive value, "
"calculated as TN/(TN+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged "
"groups. Here, TN denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative "
"items) and FN denotes false negatives (incorrectly classified negative "
"items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状が正しく変わらないま"
"ま(すなわち正しく陰性と分類されること)である対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等"
"しくなることです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような"
"人の場合もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"陰性的中率の等価性は陰性的中率にもとづき、TN/(TN+FN) として特権群と非特権群の"
"両方について計算します。ここで TN は真陰性(正しく陰性と分類された対象)、FN は"
"偽陰性(誤って陰性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups correctly experiencing changes and correctly experiencing "
"no changes in the status quo (i.e., being correctly classified as positive "
"and being correctly classified as negative). The term items refers to what "
"is being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"Accuracy parity is based on accuracy, calculated as (TP+TN)/N, applied to "
"both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, TP denotes true positives "
"(correctly classified positive items), TN denotes true negatives (correctly "
"classified negative items), and N represents the total number of items "
"classified by the algorithm. The sum of TP and TN reflects the total number "
"of correct classifications made by the algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Further Details:</u>\n"
"Accuracy parity, like accuracy as a model evaluation metric, has a major "
"flaw when applied to cases where the positive class is a small minority. For "
"example, if %1$s%% of the privileged group and %2$s%% of the unprivileged "
"group commit fraud, accuracy may seem high overall (%3$s%%), but masks "
"disparities, with the unprivileged group having lower accuracy (%4$s%%) "
"compared to the privileged group (%5$s%%). Unlike other measures, accuracy "
"parity does not consider varying error costs. It fails to detect increases "
"in false negatives or false positives, missing the associated rise in costs."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状が正しく変わる場合と"
"正しく変わらない場合(すなわち正しく陽性と分類されること、および正しく陰性と分"
"類されること)の対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等しくなることです。ここでいう「"
"対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合もあれば、銀行口座のよ"
"うな物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"正解率の等価性は正解率にもとづき、(TP+TN)/N として特権群と非特権群の両方につ"
"いて計算します。ここで TP は真陽性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)、TN は真陰性"
"(正しく陰性と分類された対象)、N はアルゴリズムが分類した対象の総数を表します"
"。TP と TN の和は、アルゴリズムが正しく分類した総数を表します。\n"
"\n"
"<u>補足:</u>\n"
"正解率の等価性は、モデル評価指標としての正解率と同じく、陽性クラスがごく少数"
"である場合に大きな欠点があります。たとえば特権群の %1$s%%、非特権群の %2$s%% "
"が不正を行っている場合、全体の正解率は高く見えます (%3$s%%) が、格差は覆い隠"
"され、非特権群の正解率 (%4$s%%) は特権群 (%5$s%%) より低くなります。ほかの指"
"標と違い、正解率の等価性は誤りの種類ごとのコストの違いを考慮しません。偽陰性"
"や偽陽性の増加を検出できず、それに伴うコストの増加を見逃します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups experiencing incorrect changes in the status quo (i.e., "
"being incorrectly classified as positive). The term items refers to what is "
"being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"False positive rate parity is based on the false positive rate, calculated "
"as FP/(TN+FP), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, FP "
"denotes false positives (incorrectly classified positive items), and TN "
"denotes true negatives (correctly classified negative items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状の誤った変化(すなわち"
"誤って陽性と分類されること)を経験する対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等しくなる"
"ことです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような人の場合"
"もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"偽陽性率の等価性は偽陽性率にもとづき、FP/(TN+FP) として特権群と非特権群の両方"
"について計算します。ここで FP は偽陽性(誤って陽性と分類された対象)、TN は真陰"
"性(正しく陰性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid ""
"<u>Definition of Fairness:</u>\n"
"The algorithm is fair if its use results in the same number of items from "
"different groups incorrectly experiencing no changes in the status quo (i."
"e., being incorrectly classified as negative). The term items refers to what "
"is being classified; these items can be people, like job applicants, or "
"objects, such as bank accounts.\n"
"\n"
"<u>Formula:</u>\n"
"False negative rate parity is based on the false negative rate, calculated "
"as FN/(TP+FN), applied to both privileged and unprivileged groups. Here, FN "
"denotes false negatives (incorrectly classified negative items), and TP "
"denotes true positives (correctly classified positive items)."
msgstr ""
"<u>公平性の定義:</u>\n"
"このアルゴリズムが公平であるとは、それを使った結果、現状が誤って変わらないま"
"ま(すなわち誤って陰性と分類されること)である対象の数が、異なる群のあいだで等"
"しくなることです。ここでいう「対象」とは分類されるものを指し、求職者のような"
"人の場合もあれば、銀行口座のような物の場合もあります。\n"
"\n"
"<u>式:</u>\n"
"偽陰性率の等価性は偽陰性率にもとづき、FN/(TP+FN) として特権群と非特権群の両方"
"について計算します。ここで FN は偽陰性(誤って陰性と分類された対象)、TP は真陽"
"性(正しく陽性と分類された対象)を表します。"

msgid "Decision-Making Workflow Plot"
msgstr "意思決定の流れのプロット"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %1$i.</b> Graphical representation of the decision-making "
"workflow. The label 'FP' indicates 'False Positives' and the label 'FN' "
"indicates 'False Negatives'. The white rectangles indicate the followed path "
"based on the answers provided to the necessary questions of the workflow, "
"the gray rectangles represent the ignored path."
msgstr ""
"<b>図 %1$i.</b> 意思決定の流れを図示したものです。ラベル 'FP' は「偽陽性」"
"、'FN' は「偽陰性」を表します。白い長方形は、流れの中の必要な問いへの回答にも"
"とづいてたどった経路を、灰色の長方形は通らなかった経路を表します。"

msgid ""
"This procedure analyzes the frequency with which values get repeated within "
"a data set to statistically identify whether the data were likely tampered "
"with. Unlike Benford's law, and its generalizations, this approach examines "
"the entire number at once, not only the first or last digit.\n"
"\n"
"To determine whether the data show an excessive amount of repeated values, "
"the null hypothesis that the data do not contain an unexpected amount of "
"repeated values is tested with a type-I error of %1$s. To quantify what is "
"expected, this test requires the assumption that the integer portions of the "
"numbers are not associated with their decimal portions."
msgstr ""
"この手順は、データセット内で値がどれくらい繰り返し現れるかを分析し、データが"
"改ざんされた可能性を統計的に調べるものです。ベンフォードの法則やその一般化と"
"違い、この方法は先頭や末尾の桁だけでなく、数値全体を一度に調べます。\n"
"\n"
"データに過剰な繰り返し値があるかを判定するため、「データに想定外の量の繰り返"
"し値は含まれない」という帰無仮説を、第1種の誤りの確率 %1$s で検定します。期待"
"される量を数値化するにあたり、この検定は数値の整数部と小数部が関連していない"
"という仮定を必要とします。"

msgid "<u>Assessing repeated values</u>"
msgstr "<u>繰り返し値を評価する</u>"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Repeated Values Test"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i.</b> 繰り返し値の検定"

msgid "Average"
msgstr "平均"

msgid "Frequency"
msgstr "頻度"

msgid "Entropy"
msgstr "エントロピー"

msgid ""
"The displayed <i>p</i>-value is one-sided and is computed on the basis of "
"%1$s samples."
msgstr ""
"表示されている <i>p</i>値は片側であり、%1$s 個の標本にもとづいて計算されてい"
"ます。"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Assumption Checks"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i.</b> 仮定のチェック"

msgid ""
"The displayed <i>p</i>-value is for a two-sided test against H%1$s: <i>r</i> "
"= 0."
msgstr "表示されている <i>p</i>値は、H%1$s: <i>r</i> = 0 に対する両側検定のものです。"

msgid "Percentage"
msgstr "パーセンテージ"

msgid "Observed vs. Expected Average Frequency"
msgstr "観測されたパーセンテージ vs. 期待されたパーセンテージ"

msgid "Average frequency"
msgstr "頻度"

msgid "Simulated frequency"
msgstr "シミュレートされた頻度"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %i:</b> The expected average frequencies of values versus the "
"observed average frequency in the data set."
msgstr ""
"<b>図 %i:</b> 値の期待される平均頻度と、データセットで観測された平均頻度の比"
"較です。"

msgid "Observed vs. Expected Entropy"
msgstr "観測されたパーセンテージ vs. 期待されたパーセンテージ"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %i:</b> The expected entropy of values versus the observed entropy "
"in the data set."
msgstr ""
"<b>図 %i:</b> 値の期待されるエントロピーと、データセットで観測された"
"エントロピーの比較です。"

msgid "Histogram of Individual Values"
msgstr "個々の値のヒストグラム"

msgid "<b>Figure %i:</b> Histogram of the individual values in the data set."
msgstr "<b>図 %i:</b> データセット内の個々の値のヒストグラムです。"

msgid "%1$s < α"
msgstr "%1$s < α"

msgid "%1$s >= α"
msgstr "%1$s >= α"

msgid ""
"The <i>p</i>-value is %1$s and the null hypothesis that the data do not "
"contain an unexpected amount of repeated values %2$s."
msgstr ""
"<i>p</i>値は %1$s であり、データに予期しないほどの反復値 %2$s が含まれていな"
"い帰無仮説."

msgid "percentage"
msgstr "パーセンテージ"

msgid "amount"
msgstr "量"

msgid "<u>Planning</u>"
msgstr "<u>計画</u>"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The materiality is higher than, or equal to the total "
"value of the observations."
msgstr "分析できません: 重要性が観測値の合計額以上になっています。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The expected errors are equal to, or higher than, the "
"number of units in the population."
msgstr "分析できません: 期待誤謬数が母集団の単位数以上になっています。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The expected errors are higher than the performance "
"materiality."
msgstr "分析できません: 期待誤謬数が手続実施上の重要性を超えています。"

msgid ""
"The detection risk is equal to or higher than 100%%. Please re-specify the "
"custom values for the Inherent risk and/or Control risk and/or Analytical "
"risk, or the confidence."
msgstr ""
"発見リスクが 100%% 以上になっています。固有リスク・統制リスク・分析的リスクの"
"カスタム値、または信頼度を指定し直してください。"

msgid ""
"You cannot incorporate this prior information into your analysis because you "
"are not testing against a performance materiality."
msgstr ""
"手続実施上の重要性に対する検定を行っていないため、この事前情報を分析に取り込"
"むことはできません。"

msgid ""
"The prior expected misstatement rate in the population is larger than the "
"performance materiality."
msgstr "母集団における事前の期待誤記載率が、手続実施上の重要性を超えています。"

msgid "Selection Summary"
msgstr "抽出の要約"

msgid ""
"You must specify unique item ID's. The row numbers of the data set are "
"sufficient."
msgstr "項目に一意なIDを指定してください。データセットの行番号でも十分です。"

msgid "Evaluation Summary"
msgstr "評価の要約"

msgid ""
"The hypergeometric upper bound requires that you specify the number of units "
"in the population."
msgstr "超幾何分布による上限を求めるには、母集団の単位数を指定する必要があります。"

msgid ""
"The direct, difference, ratio, and regression bounds require that you "
"specify the number of items and the number of units in the population."
msgstr ""
"直接推定・差分推定・比率推定・回帰推定による上限を求めるには、母集団の項目数"
"と単位数を指定する必要があります。"

msgid ""
"The detection risk is equal to or higher than 100%%. Please re-specify your "
"values for the Inherent risk and/or Control risk and/or Analytical risk, or "
"the confidence."
msgstr ""
"発見リスクが 100%% 以上になっています。固有リスク・統制リスク・分析的リスクの"
"値、または信頼度を指定し直してください。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The materiality (%1$s) is higher than, or equal to "
"the total value of the population (%2$s)."
msgstr "分析できません: 重要性 (%1$s) が母集団の合計額 (%2$s) 以上になっています。"

msgid ""
"Analysis not possible: The hurdle model cannot be applied with this specific "
"prior distribution because it is improper. Please specify a different prior "
"distribution."
msgstr ""
"分析できません: 指定された事前分布は非正則なので、ハードルモデルを適用できま"
"せん。別の事前分布を指定してください。"

msgid ""
"Select one or both sampling objectives to begin planning an audit sample.\n"
"\n"
"%1$s <b>Test against a performance materiality</b>\n"
"\n"
"Enable this objective if you want to test whether the total misstatement in "
"the population exceeds a certain limit (i.e., the performance materiality) "
"based on a sample. This approach allows you to plan a sample such that, when "
"the sample meets your expectations, the maximum error is said to be below "
"performance materiality. In the evaluation you will be able to quantify the "
"evidence that your sample contains for or against the statement that the "
"population misstatement does not exceed the performance materiality.\n"
"\n"
"%2$s <b>Obtain a minimum precision</b>\n"
"\n"
"Enable this objective if you want to obtain a minimum precision when "
"estimating the total misstatement in the population based on a sample. This "
"approach allows you to plan a sample such that, when the sample meets "
"expectations, the accuracy of your estimate is below a tolerable percentage. "
"In the evaluation you will be able to quantify the accuracy of your estimate "
"of the population misstatement."
msgstr ""
"監査標本の計画を始めるには、抽出の目的を1つまたは両方選んでください。\n"
"\n"
"%1$s <b>手続実施上の重要性に対する検定</b>\n"
"\n"
"母集団の誤記載の合計が一定の限度(すなわち手続実施上の重要性)を超えるかどうか"
"を標本にもとづいて検定したい場合は、この目的を有効にします。この方法では、標"
"本が期待どおりであれば最大誤謬が手続実施上の重要性を下回るといえるように標本"
"を計画できます。評価の段階では、母集団の誤記載が手続実施上の重要性を超えない"
"という主張に対して、標本がどれだけの証拠をもつかを数値化できます。\n"
"\n"
"%2$s <b>最小精度の確保</b>\n"
"\n"
"標本にもとづいて母集団の誤記載の合計を推定する際に、最小精度を確保したい場合"
"は、この目的を有効にします。この方法では、標本が期待どおりであれば推定の正確"
"さが許容できる割合を下回るように標本を計画できます。評価の段階では、母集団の"
"誤記載についての推定の正確さを数値化できます。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to show with %1$s confidence "
"that the %2$s of misstatement in the population is lower than the "
"performance materiality of %3$s."
msgstr ""
"この抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載の %2$s が手続実施上の重要性 %3$s を下回"
"ることを、%1$s の信頼度で示すことです。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to estimate the misstatement in "
"the population with %1$s confidence and a minimum precision of %2$s.\n"
"\n"
"The quantity of interest is the misstatement θ in the population. "
"Misstatement is defined as the difference between an item's booked "
"(recorded) value and its audited (true) value."
msgstr ""
"この抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載を %1$s の信頼度と %2$s の最小精度で推定"
"することです。\n"
"\n"
"関心のある量は母集団の誤記載 θ です。誤記載とは、項目の計上(記録)された値と、"
"監査後の(真の)値との差を指します。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this sampling procedure is to show with %1$s confidence and "
"a precision of %3$s that the %2$s of misstatement in the population is lower "
"than the performance materiality of %4$s."
msgstr ""
"この抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載の %2$s が手続実施上の重要性 %4$s を下回"
"ることを、%1$s の信頼度と %3$s の精度で示すことです。"

msgid "of intolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "許容できない誤記載 H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of exact misstatement H%1$s: %2$s = %3$s"
msgstr "正確な誤記載 H%1$s: %2$s = %3$s"

msgid "of tolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "許容できる誤記載 H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of tolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s < %3$s"
msgstr "許容できる誤記載 H%1$s: %2$s < %3$s"

msgid "of no misstatement H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"
msgstr "誤記載なし H%1$s: %2$s %3$s %4$s"

msgid "of intolerable misstatement H%1$s: %2$s > %3$s"
msgstr "許容できない誤記載 H%1$s: %2$s > %3$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"The quantity of interest is the misstatement %2$s in the population. "
"Misstatement is defined as the difference between an item's booked "
"(recorded) value and its audit (true) value. When testing the population "
"misstatement against a given performance materiality, two statistical "
"hypotheses about %2$s are formulated:\n"
"\n"
"- The (null) hypothesis %3$s,\n"
"- The (alternative) hypothesis %4$s.\n"
"\n"
"The audit risk %5$s is the risk of incorrectly rejecting the hypothesis "
"%3$s. To reject this hypothesis on the basis of a sample, the information "
"from the sample must be sufficient to reduce %5$s to an appropriately low "
"level (i.e., %5$s < %6$s%%)."
msgstr ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"関心のある量は母集団の誤記載 %2$s です。誤記載とは、項目の計上(記録)された値"
"と、監査後の(真の)値との差を指します。母集団の誤記載を所定の手続実施上の重要"
"性に対して検定するとき、%2$s について2つの統計的仮説を立てます。\n"
"\n"
"- (帰無)仮説 %3$s\n"
"- (対立)仮説 %4$s\n"
"\n"
"監査リスク %5$s は、仮説 %3$s を誤って棄却するリスクです。標本にもとづいてこ"
"の仮説を棄却するには、%5$s を十分に低い水準まで下げられるだけの情報が標本から"
"得られなければなりません(すなわち %5$s < %6$s%%)。"

msgid ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"In a Bayesian analysis, the parameter %2$s is assigned a prior probability "
"distribution that incorporates the available audit information about the "
"misstatement in the population."
msgstr ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"ベイズ分析では、パラメータ %2$s に事前確率分布を割り当てます。この事前分布は"
"、母集団の誤記載について利用できる監査情報を反映したものです。"

msgid "a performance materiality of %1$s"
msgstr "手続実施上の重要性 %1$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to conclude that the misstatement "
"in the population is below the performance materiality"
msgstr ""
"母集団の誤記載が手続実施上の重要性を下回ると結論するのに十分な情報が標本から"
"得られます"

msgid "a minimum precision of %1$s"
msgstr "最小精度 %1$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to estimate the misstatement in "
"the population with the minimum precision"
msgstr "母集団の誤記載を最小精度で推定するのに十分な情報が標本から得られます"

msgid "a performance materiality of %1$s and a minimum precision of %2$s"
msgstr "手続実施上の重要性 %1$s と最小精度 %2$s"

msgid ""
"the sample provides sufficient information to conclude that the misstatement "
"in the population is below the performance materiality with the minimum "
"precision"
msgstr ""
"母集団の誤記載が手続実施上の重要性を下回ると最小精度で結論するのに十分な情報"
"が標本から得られます"

msgid ""
"Furthermore, the uncertainty regarding θ will only be extrapolated over the "
"unseen part of the population. This requires the additional assumption that "
"the population taints are homogeneous."
msgstr ""
"さらに、θ についての不確実性は母集団の未検査部分にのみ外挿されます。これには"
"、母集団の汚染度が均質であるという追加の仮定が必要です。"

msgid "gamma"
msgstr "ガンマ"

msgid "beta"
msgstr "ベータ"

msgid "beta-binomial"
msgstr "ベータ二項"

msgid ""
"The purpose of the planning stage is to find a minimum sample size so that, "
"given a certain number of expected misstatements, the sample provides "
"sufficient information to achieve the specified sampling objectives."
msgstr ""
"計画段階の目的は、一定の期待誤記載数のもとで、指定した抽出の目的を達成するの"
"に十分な情報が標本から得られるような、最小のサンプルサイズを見つけることです"
"。"

msgid ""
"No assumptions are made about the most likely expected error in the sample."
msgstr "標本で最も起こりやすい期待誤謬について、仮定は置きません。"

msgid "The most likely expected error in the sample is expected to be %1$s."
msgstr "標本で最も起こりやすい期待誤謬は %1$s と見込まれます。"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that every value of the misstatement "
"is equally likely, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr ""
"%1$s%2$s %3$s に必要な最小サンプルサイズは、標本に %4$s 件の誤謬が含まれると"
"仮定すると %5$s です。このサンプルサイズは %6$s 分布、誤記載のどの値も等しく"
"起こりやすいという事前の仮定、および与えられた期待誤謬数にもとづいています"
"。\n"
"\n"
"したがって、意図した標本を評価した結果、監査した項目の(比例)誤記載の合計が "
"%7$s 以下であれば、%8$s。%9$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assessments of inherent risk (<i>%7$s</i>), "
"control risk (<i>%8$s</i>) and analytical risk (<i>%9$s</i>) from the Audit "
"Risk Model, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %10$s, %11$s. %12$s"
msgstr ""
"%1$s%2$s %3$s に必要な最小サンプルサイズは、標本に %4$s 件の誤謬が含まれると"
"仮定すると %5$s です。このサンプルサイズは %6$s 分布、監査リスクモデルによる"
"固有リスク (<i>%7$s</i>)・統制リスク (<i>%8$s</i>)・分析的リスク (<i>%9$s</"
"i>) の事前評価、および与えられた期待誤謬数にもとづいています。\n"
"\n"
"したがって、意図した標本を評価した結果、監査した項目の(比例)誤記載の合計が "
"%10$s 以下であれば、%11$s。%12$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that tolerable misstatement is equally "
"likely to occur as intolerable misstatement, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr ""
"%1$s%2$s %3$s に必要な最小サンプルサイズは、標本に %4$s 件の誤謬が含まれると"
"仮定すると %5$s です。このサンプルサイズは %6$s 分布、許容できる誤記載と許容"
"できない誤記載が等しく起こりやすいという事前の仮定、および与えられた期待誤謬"
"数にもとづいています。\n"
"\n"
"したがって、意図した標本を評価した結果、監査した項目の(比例)誤記載の合計が "
"%7$s 以下であれば、%8$s。%9$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the a priori assumption that an earlier sample of %7$s "
"transactions containing %8$s errors is seen, and the given expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %9$s, %10$s. %11$s"
msgstr ""
"%1$s%2$s %3$s に必要な最小サンプルサイズは、標本に %4$s 件の誤謬が含まれると"
"仮定すると %5$s です。このサンプルサイズは %6$s 分布、%7$s 件の取引のうち "
"%8$s 件の誤謬を含む先行標本を観測したという事前の仮定、および与えられた期待誤"
"謬数にもとづいています。\n"
"\n"
"したがって、意図した標本を評価した結果、監査した項目の(比例)誤記載の合計が "
"%9$s 以下であれば、%10$s。%11$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s%2$s The minimum sample size that is required for %3$s, assuming the "
"sample contains %4$s errors, is %5$s. This sample size is based on the %6$s "
"distribution, the manually specified prior distribution, and the given "
"expected errors.\n"
"\n"
"Consequently, if the intended sample is evaluated and the sum of "
"(proportional) misstatements in the audited items is lower than (or equal "
"to) %7$s, %8$s. %9$s"
msgstr ""
"%1$s%2$s %3$s に必要な最小サンプルサイズは、標本に %4$s 件の誤謬が含まれると"
"仮定すると %5$s です。このサンプルサイズは %6$s 分布、手動で指定した事前分布"
"、および与えられた期待誤謬数にもとづいています。\n"
"\n"
"したがって、意図した標本を評価した結果、監査した項目の(比例)誤記載の合計が "
"%7$s 以下であれば、%8$s。%9$s"

msgid "random"
msgstr "変量"

msgid "fixed interval"
msgstr "固定間隔"

msgid "cell"
msgstr "セル"

msgid "sieve"
msgstr "ふるい"

msgid "book values (<i>%1$s</i>)"
msgstr "簿価 (<i>%1$s</i>)"

msgid "book values (<i>...</i>)"
msgstr "簿価 (<i>...</i>)"

msgid "ID variable (<i>%1$s</i>)"
msgstr "ID変数 (<i>%1$s</i>)"

msgid "ID variable (<i>...</i>)"
msgstr "ID変数 (<i>...</i>)"

msgid ""
"<br><b>Warning:</b> A monetary unit sampling method was tried but failed."
msgstr "<br><b>警告:</b> 金額単位抽出法を試みましたが失敗しました。"

msgid "%1$s record sampling"
msgstr "%1$s レコード抽出"

msgid "%1$s monetary unit sampling"
msgstr "%1$s 金額単位抽出"

msgid "items"
msgstr "項目"

msgid "monetary units"
msgstr "金額単位"

msgid "randomized"
msgstr "無作為化"

msgid "non-randomized"
msgstr "非無作為化"

msgid ""
"The purpose of the selection stage is to statistically select a number of "
"sampling units from the population. Sampling units can be individual items "
"(rows) or individual monetary units. The sampling units are selected from "
"the population according to the selection method. To learn more about the "
"current selection method, look under the <i>Method</i> section.\n"
"\n"
"From the population of %1$s %2$s items, %3$s sampling units (%4$s) are "
"selected from the %5$s using the %6$s method.%7$s"
msgstr ""
"抽出段階の目的は、母集団から一定数の抽出単位を統計的に選び出すことです。抽出"
"単位は個々の項目(行)の場合もあれば、個々の金額単位の場合もあります。抽出単位"
"は、抽出方法に従って母集団から選ばれます。現在の抽出方法について詳しくは <i>"
"方法</i> の節をご覧ください。\n"
"\n"
"%1$s %2$s 件の項目からなる母集団から、%6$s 法を使って %5$s から %3$s 件の抽出"
"単位 (%4$s) が選ばれました。%7$s"

msgid ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"<b>Note:</b> The selected sample (%2$s) contains fewer items than the "
"planned sample size (%3$s) because some items are selected more than once. "
"The items containing these %4$s extra selected sampling units will be "
"counted multiple times in the evaluation."
msgstr ""
"%1$s\n"
"\n"
"<b>注:</b> 選ばれた標本 (%2$s) は、計画されたサンプルサイズ (%3$s) より項目数"
"が少なくなっています。同じ項目が複数回選ばれているためです。この %4$s 件の余"
"分に選ばれた抽出単位を含む項目は、評価の際に複数回数えられます。"

msgid "overall materiality"
msgstr "全体としての重要性"

msgid ""
"Furthermore, an overall materiality of %1$s was determined and is used to "
"evaluate the population misstatement."
msgstr ""
"さらに、全体としての重要性 %1$s が決められ、母集団の誤記載の評価に使われます"
"。"

msgid "performance materiality"
msgstr "手続実施上の重要性"

msgid "below"
msgstr "下回る"

msgid "lower"
msgstr "下限"

msgid "above"
msgstr "上回る"

msgid "higher"
msgstr "高い"

msgid "<b>Objectives:</b> You have achieved your initial sampling objectives."
msgstr "<b>目的:</b> 当初の抽出の目的を達成しました。"

msgid ""
"<b>Objectives:</b> You have not achieved your initial sampling objectives."
msgstr "<b>目的:</b> 当初の抽出の目的を達成できませんでした。"

msgid ""
"The objective of this audit sampling procedure was to determine with %1$s "
"confidence whether the misstatement in the population is lower than the "
"specified performance materiality, in this case %2$s. %3$sFor the current "
"data, the %1$s upper bound for the misstatement is %4$s the %5$s. \n"
"\n"
"The conclusion on the basis of these results is that the misstatement in the "
"population is %6$s than the %5$s. %7$s"
msgstr ""
"この監査抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載が指定された手続実施上の重要性(この場"
"合 %2$s)を下回るかどうかを、%1$s の信頼度で判定することでした。%3$s現在の"
"データでは、誤記載の %1$s 上限は %5$s を %4$s 値です。\n"
"\n"
"この結果にもとづく結論は、母集団の誤記載が %5$s を %6$s ということです。%7$s"

msgid ""
"The objective of this audit sampling procedure was to determine the "
"misstatement in the population with %1$s confidence and a minimum precision "
"of %2$s. For the current data, the obtained precision is %3$s than the "
"minimum precision. \n"
"\n"
"The conclusion on the basis of these results is that the misstatement in the "
"population has been determined with at least %1$s confidence and a precision "
"of %4$s. %5$s"
msgstr ""
"この監査抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載を %1$s の信頼度と %2$s の最小精度で"
"判定することでした。現在のデータでは、得られた精度は最小精度より %3$s 値です"
"。\n"
"\n"
"この結果にもとづく結論は、母集団の誤記載が少なくとも %1$s の信頼度と %4$s の"
"精度で判定されたということです。%5$s"

msgid ""
"The objective of this audit sampling procedure was to determine with %1$s "
"confidence, and a minimum precision of %2$s, whether the misstatement in the "
"population is lower than the specified performance materiality, in this case "
"%3$s. %4$sFor the current data, the %1$s upper bound for the misstatement is "
"%5$s the %6$s and the obtained precision is %7$s than the minimum "
"precision. \n"
"\n"
"The conclusion on the basis of these results is that, with a precision of "
"%8$s, the misstatement in the population is %9$s than the %6$s. %10$s"
msgstr ""
"この監査抽出手続の目的は、母集団の誤記載が指定された手続実施上の重要性(この場"
"合 %3$s)を下回るかどうかを、%1$s の信頼度と %2$s の最小精度で判定することでし"
"た。%4$s現在のデータでは、誤記載の %1$s 上限は %6$s を %5$s 値であり、得られ"
"た精度は最小精度より %7$s 値です。\n"
"\n"
"この結果にもとづく結論は、精度 %8$s のもとで母集団の誤記載が %6$s を %9$s と"
"いうことです。%10$s"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Descriptive Statistics for Book Values"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i.</b> 簿価の記述統計"

msgid "Population size"
msgstr "母集団のサイズ"

msgid "Absolute value"
msgstr "絶対値"

msgid "Mean"
msgstr "平均値"

msgid "Std. deviation"
msgstr "標準偏差"

msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

msgid "Quartile"
msgstr "四分位数"

msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

msgid "3"
msgstr "3"

msgid "Distribution of Book Values"
msgstr "簿価の分布"

msgid "Mean ± St.dev"
msgstr "平均 ± 標準偏差"

msgid ""
"<b>Figure %1$i.</b> The distribution of book values in the population. The "
"red and blue dots respectively represent the mean and the values exactly one "
"standard deviation from the mean. The orange dots represent the first, "
"second (median) and third quartiles of the book values."
msgstr ""
"<b>図 %1$i.</b> 母集団における簿価の分布です。赤い点は平均、青い点は平均から"
"ちょうど標準偏差1つ分離れた値を表します。オレンジ色の点は簿価の第1・第2(中央"
"値)・第3四分位数を表します。"

msgid "High"
msgstr "高い"

msgid "Medium"
msgstr "中程度"

msgid "Low"
msgstr "低い"

msgid "<u>Audit Risk Model</u>"
msgstr "<u>監査リスクモデル</u>"

msgid ""
"The Audit Risk Model is a method to reduce the required information from the "
"sample on the basis of earlier assessments of inherent risk, control risk "
"and analytical risk, while maintaining the desired audit risk.\n"
"\n"
"Prior to the sampling procedure, the inherent risk was determined to be "
"%1$s, the control risk was determined to be %2$s and the analytical risk was "
"determined to be %3$s. According to the Audit Risk Model, the required "
"detection risk to maintain an audit risk of %4$s should be %5$s."
msgstr ""
"監査リスクモデルは、固有リスク・統制リスク・分析的リスクの事前評価にもとづい"
"て、望ましい監査リスクを保ちながら、標本に必要な情報量を減らす方法です。\n"
"\n"
"抽出手続に先立ち、固有リスクは %1$s、統制リスクは %2$s、分析的リスクは %3$s "
"と判断されました。監査リスクモデルによれば、監査リスクを %4$s に保つために必"
"要な発見リスクは %5$s となります。"

msgid ""
"Audit risk (%1$s%%) = Inherent risk (%2$s%%) x Control risk (%3$s%%) x "
"Analytical Risk (%4$s%%) x Detection risk (%5$s%%)"
msgstr ""
"監査リスク (%1$s%%) = 固有リスク (%2$s%%) × 統制リスク (%3$s%%) × 分析的"
"リスク (%4$s%%) × 発見リスク (%5$s%%)"

msgid ""
"At least one translation of the categories High, Medium and Low to "
"probabilities is done according custom settings."
msgstr ""
"「高」「中」「低」のカテゴリから確率への変換のうち、少なくとも1つはカスタム設"
"定に従っています。"

msgid ""
"The translation of the categories high, medium and low to probabilities is "
"done using the default settings shown in the table below."
msgstr ""
"「高」「中」「低」のカテゴリから確率への変換は、下の表に示す既定の設定を使っ"
"ています。"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Default Settings Audit Risk Model"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i.</b> 監査リスクモデルの既定設定"

msgid "Inherent risk"
msgstr "固有リスク"

msgid "Control risk"
msgstr "統制リスク"

msgid "Analytical risk"
msgstr "分析的リスク"

msgid "= Selected"
msgstr "= 選択"

msgid ""
"The detection risk is equal to or higher than 100%%. Please re-specify the "
"percentages for the Inherent risk and/or Control risk and/or Analytical risk."
msgstr ""
"発見リスクが 100%% 以上になっています。固有リスク・統制リスク・分析的リスクの"
"割合を指定し直してください。"

msgid ""
"You cannot achieve your current sampling objectives with this population. "
"The resulting sample size exceeds the maximum of %1$s. Adjust the maximum "
"option accordingly."
msgstr ""
"この母集団では現在の抽出の目的を達成できません。得られるサンプルサイズが上限"
"の %1$s を超えています。上限のオプションを適宜調整してください。"

msgid ""
"The tolerable misstatements are larger than the performance materiality. If "
"you used an absolute number of tolerable misstatements < 1, please use the "
"'relative' option."
msgstr ""
"許容できる誤記載が手続実施上の重要性を超えています。許容できる誤記載として 1 "
"未満の絶対数を指定した場合は、「相対」のオプションを使ってください。"

msgid "<b>Table %1$i.</b> Planning Summary"
msgstr "<b>表 %1$i.</b> 計画の要約"

msgid "Performance materiality"
msgstr "手続実施上の重要性"

msgid "Min. precision"
msgstr "最小精度"

msgid "Detection risk"
msgstr "発見リスク"

msgid "Audit risk"
msgstr "監査リスク"

msgid "Tolerable misstatements"
msgstr "許容できる誤記載"

msgid "Minimum sample size"
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズ"

msgid "The minimum sample size is based on the Poisson distribution."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズはポアソン分布にもとづいています。"

msgid "The minimum sample size is based on the binomial distribution."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズは二項分布にもとづいています。"

msgid "The minimum sample size is based on the hypergeometric distribution."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズは超幾何分布にもとづいています。"

msgid "The minimum sample size is based on the gamma distribution."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズはガンマ分布にもとづいています。"

msgid "The minimum sample size is based on the beta distribution."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズはベータ分布にもとづいています。"

msgid ""
"The minimum sample size is based on the beta-binomial distribution (N = "
"%1$s)."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズはベータ二項分布にもとづいています (N = %1$s)。"

msgid ""
"Either the materiality (if applicable) or the number of units in the "
"population is defined as zero."
msgstr "重要性(該当する場合)または母集団の単位数が 0 に設定されています。"

msgid "%1$s <b>Insufficient information.</b>"
msgstr "%1$s <b>情報が不十分です。</b>"

msgid ""
"The minimum sample size is based on the Poisson distribution (%1$s = %2$s)."
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズはポアソン分布にもとづいています (%1$s = %2$s)。"

msgid ""
"The minimum sample size is based on the binomial distribution (p = %1$s)"
msgstr "最小サンプルサイズは二項分布にもとづいています (p = %1$s)"

msgid ""
